                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Table 4 shows the distribution of emotional intensity labels. For all emotions, intensity 0 is most frequently assigned. This is not surprising, as it is rare for a single post to come with many emotions, which may be contradictory to each other, at the same time. $ ^{11} $ However, for emotions of anger and trust, about 95% of labels by the objective annotators have an intensity 0, which is particularly high. In other words, with regard to emotions of anger and trust, readers may tend to underestimate the emotions of the writers. In addition, we can see some characteristics of each objective annotator, e.g., the number of times that reader 1 gives intensity 1 is small.",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                778,
                585,
                1159
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 67,
            "global_group_id": 67,
            "block_polygon_points": [
